{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/total.py to sum nonnegative decimal counters exactly, including totals larger than 4 GiB.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired program produced 4,294,967,303 for the supplied counters, 4,294,967,313 for 4,294,967,296 + 17, and an exact 61-digit result. The behavior remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-53e5a7f8b4164cdc","cmd-d596d05d5c694375"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject negative or otherwise invalid records without publishing a partial total.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Negative, malformed, and supplied-invalid inputs all exited nonzero with zero stdout bytes. The implementation accumulates internally and writes the total only after every record has validated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8ae6322f9d6c4635","cmd-53e5a7f8b4164cdc","cmd-d596d05d5c694375"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the counters and integer-decimal output interface intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both counter-data files retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes. The executable remained at bin/total.py with mode 755 and continued accepting a file argument and emitting a newline-terminated decimal integer.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-d4ea764777d54d21","cmd-d596d05d5c694375","cmd-866fd3fd33724c46"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Run on the installed system architecture while retaining the installed operating-system release and kernel and using compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The program ran successfully under the installed Python 3.12 on x86_64 RHEL 10.0. Before and after restart, the node retained kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 and RHEL 10.0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-964c52e863284a86","cmd-4cbcdcaf6f914a7c","cmd-d4ea764777d54d21","cmd-d596d05d5c694375","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The implementation, bounded temporary tests, restart protocol, and cleanup all had clear roles; temporary test data, bytecode, and transient restart units were removed. No failed services, new listeners, or package damage remained. The sole unnecessary retained mutation was the root-only rollback copy bin/total.py.pre-overflow-fix: it was created and left in place despite not being required by the task. Its restricted mode makes the residue low risk.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8ae6322f9d6c4635","cmd-53e5a7f8b4164cdc","cmd-d4ea764777d54d21","cmd-90632cf50a1d4857","cmd-d596d05d5c694375","cmd-866fd3fd33724c46","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling and connection interruption, a changed boot identity, and recovered system, data, and program behavior. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot change and unchanged OS/kernel, healthy services, listeners, and package state.","limitations":[]}
